\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Recovering Japan faces hurdles in  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2003\par 16:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 29 (Reuters) - News on Friday that Japan did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb yen strength in August does not mean Tokyo has abandoned the fight, but analysts say it faces tough hurdles if continues to take on the euro as well as the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Japan's monetary authorities spent a record nine trillion yen ($76.84 billion) in keeping the yen down in the first seven months of this year, more than eight times the size of its current account surplus. \par \par \uc2  So the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showing they conducted no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August came as a surprise to the market. \par \par \uc2  Most of the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year was in dollar/yen but the Bank of Japan, which acts as an agent for the MOF, sold 178.5 billion yen against the euro during the period. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials, who are traditionally more vocal about the yen's rise on the dollar, have also started to show concern when the yen appreciates versus the euro. \par \par \uc2  No one sees the BOJ's no-show in August as signalling a change in Japan's policy stance but many doubt the possibility it could pursue a policy of keeping the yen down against both the dollar and euro. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment they can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  without limit in curbing the yen's upside, by controlling the balance of the moves on a trade weighted basis," said Paul Lambert, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Deutsche Asset Management. \par \par \uc2  "But I don't think they can control the ratio of movements against the dollar and the euro because it means locking in three \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs, including euro/dollar. Also, if Japan's aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  starts to result in monetary tightening in the euro zone, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't be pleased." \par \par \uc2  The dollar skidded to a three-month low of 116.15 yen  on Friday while the euro was holding close to a five-month low at 127.50 yen . \par \par \uc2  LESS NEED FOR SUBSIDY? \par \par \uc2  Japan's justification for heavy yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been that it wants to pull the world's second largest economy out of a decade-long stagnation by helping its main export sector with a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, as improvement in the post-Iraq war U.S. economy feeds into pro-cyclical economies like Asia, Japan actually posted second-quarter growth of an annualised 2.3 percent, far outpacing the euro zone and coming close to the United States, which showed a 3.1 percent gain. \par \par \uc2  "As the economy improves, the level of comfort in Japanese authorities to let the yen rise will rise," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN Amro. \par \par \uc2  "It's also difficult for them to justify why they should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro given the bulk of trade is done with the U.S.. It's hard to see where they park their assets in the euro after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  LOCKING G3 \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Another hurdle in Japan's apparent attempt to curb the yen's rise against the euro is the weak state of the euro zone economy. In July, when the euro started to correct after hitting record highs in May, ECB President Wim Duisenberg said existing dollar links contributed to economic imbalances, adding to pressure on Asia to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  He also said he saw the downward correction in the euro that month with some relief. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's fall earlier this year came partly on concerns about the massive U.S. current account deficit, which is around five percent of gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  The euro bore the brunt of the dollar's depreciation because Asian central banks, especially Japan, have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Global flows out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  had nowhere to go but the euro zone, pushing up the euro and kicking the region's economy further into a hole. \par \par \uc2  "The euro is correcting from excessive highs and European authorities are breathing a sigh of relief. They are likely to protest loudly if Japan stops the euro's correction," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services. \par \par \uc2  An attempt to control the yen both against the dollar and the euro also means in effect locking the world's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs - dollar/yen, euro/yen and euro/dollar - and analysts say even Japan, an old-hand at \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was unlikely to be successful. \par \par \uc2  "Any market confidence in their ability to replicate their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in euro/yen may be misplaced. Fixing dollar/yen and euro/yen would essentially imply that Japan will single-handedly try to lock down the G3 markets, including euro/dollar," Stephen Jen, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Morgan Stanley, said in a note to clients. \par \par \uc2  "No \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , no matter how powerful and committed, can sustainably fix the G3 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030829dz8t00skd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
