\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar edges up in market wary of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Yoshiko Mori \par \uc2 781 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2002\par 05:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 18 (Reuters) - The dollar posted slim gains on the yen and euro by midday on Thursday on buying by traders wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese and possibly U.S. monetary authorities. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said on Thursday the ministry was always in contact with overseas authorities on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters, adding that it would take action in the market if needed. \par \par \uc2  The reference to being in touch with overseas authorities, more specific than the usual jawboning by Japanese officials to curb the yen and coming after a similar comment on Wednesday, caught the market's attention. \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan also gave traders pause for thought with unusually outspoken remarks on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in his testimony to Congress on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan said: "A considerable volume of market commentary in recent weeks has suggested that concerns about earnings prospects and the proliferating revelations of serious governance and accounting issues have contributed not only to lower equity prices but also to a decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  value of the dollar." \par \par \uc2  But he said he wanted to raise a flag of caution regarding those forecasts. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that Greenspan said much more than usual about the dollar suggested he was keen on the issue, which generated caution among traders about selling it down too far, at least for now," said Minori Takeuchi, vice president of research in the Global Trading Division of Chase Manhattan Bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT, the dollar stood at 116.50/60 yen compared to 116.31 yen in late New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the dollar tumbled to 115.50 yen a 17-month low and hit a 2-= year low against the euro of $1.0162. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0050/55 and 117.13 yen compared to $1.0070 and 117.15 yen in late U.S. trading. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the Dow ended up 0.82 percent after seven straight sessions of losses, while the Nasdaq composite index ended up 1.60 percent - but both were well below early highs posted on friendly earnings data. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan repeated his upbeat long-term outlook for the U.S. economy in his testimony to the House Financial Services Committee on Wednesday. But those comments failed to help sustain an early stock market rally or boost the dollar. \par \par \uc2  BERGSTEN SUPPORTS WEAK DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Among the chatter on the Tokyo market, one item that got attention was a commentary by influential economist Fred Bergsten, though his remarks had little effect on the dollar's value. \par \par \uc2  Bergsten, head of the Institute for International Economics, a Washington think tank, said in Thursday's Financial Times: "The dollar should be permitted to complete its necessary correction over the next year or so, with, one hopes, a trajectory as orderly as that of the past six months." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  should maintain its policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, he said, adding that the United States and its Group of Seven partners should insist that other countries refrain from taking any measures that would impede the adjustment. \par \par \uc2  Separately, White House economic adviser Glenn Hubbard told the Joint Economic Committee of Congress that the weak dollar had played a part in the current recovery of the battered U.S. manufacturing sector. \par \par \uc2  CAPITAL FLOWS AIDS DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Japanese investors made net purchases of a total of 267.2 billion yen ($2.30 billion) worth of foreign stocks in the week from July 8. It was their largest weekly purchase of foreign stocks since the Ministry began collecting weekly capflow data in April 2001. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said the large foreign stock purchases were in part due to buying by Japanese public pension funds. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0232 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls\par                                 17 Jul.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              1.0046   1.0071   -0.25   +12.83   0.8904\par  Dlr/yen               116.63   116.30   +0.28   -11.40   131.63\par  Euro/yen              117.17   117.13   +0.03    -0.06   117.24\par  Dlr/swiss             1.4570   1.4540   +0.21   -12.20   1.6594\par  Stg/dlr               1.5670   1.5703   -0.21    +7.76   1.4541\par  Can/dlr               1.5392   1.5393   -0.01    -3.30   1.5917\par  Aus/dlr               0.5515   0.5512   +0.05    +8.01   0.5106\par  Euro/swiss            1.4643   1.4652   -0.06    -0.93   1.4780\par  Euro/stg              0.6408   0.6410   -0.03    +4.65   0.6123.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020718dy7i00599\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
