\par\par \b \uc2  CHRONOLOGY-Milestones for the euro since its launch. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,027 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2002\par 13:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 15 (Reuters) - The euro rose above the psychologically key $1.00 against the U.S. dollar on Monday to establish parity for the first time since February 2000. \par \par \uc2  Following is a snapshot of the performance of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's performance dating back to its launch: \par \par \uc2  * July 15, 2002 - The euro powers above the key one-to-one level against the dollar as concern over the outlook for Wall Street encouraged investors to move out of U.S. assets. By 1112 GMT the euro had risen to $1.0007, bringing its gains against the dollar to more than 12 percent in 2002. \par \par \uc2  * July 11, 2002 - Euro zone finance ministers, EU commissioner Pedro Solbes and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vice-president Lucas Papademos issue late night formal statement saying they welcome the euro's rise and that a strong euro is in the interest of the euro area. Euro trades around $0.9880. \par \par \uc2  * June 28, 2002 - Euro hits $0.9990, highest level since Feb 2000 after U.S. office equipment maker Xerox says it expected a revenue restatement of around $2 billion over the five year period between 1997 and 2001. \par \par \uc2  * June 26, 2002 - Euro hits $0.9944, highest level since Feb 2000, a retracement of nearly 50 percent of its long-term losses from launch day highs to record lows. Euro also reaches the equivalent of three deutschemarks to the pound. Buying was accelerated by the WorldCom announcement of improper accounting. \par \par \uc2  * June 25, 2002 - U.S. telecommunications giant WorldCom reveals after U.S. trading hours improper accounting of more than $4 billion. \par \par \uc2  * June 20, 2002 - Euro rises above $0.96 for first time since June 2000, after the U.S. shows a record current account deficit in the first quarter. The weakness of U.S. assets is making it harder for the United States to attract foreign investment. \par \par \uc2  * May 22, 2002 - Euro rises above $0.92 for first time since Oct, 2001. Japan makes the first of several rounds of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the export-harming strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  * Jan 2, 2002 - The euro gains one percent against the dollar, sterling and yen in a wave of enthusiasm inspired by the smooth introduction of euro notes and coins in the 12 countries of the euro zone. Euro rises above $0.90. \par \par \uc2  * Dec 11, 2001 - U.S. Federal Reserve makes latest of 11 interest rates cuts in 2001, taking federal funds rate to 1.75 percent, the lowest for four decades. Euro closes at $0.8926. \par \par \uc2  * Dec 2, 2001 - U.S. energy giant Enron files for bankruptcy, the biggest in U.S. corporate history, after disclosing that it would write down $1.2 billion in shareholder equity due to off-balance sheet transactions. The euro closes on Dec 3 at $0.8913. \par \par \uc2  * Nov 8, 2001 - European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lowers key market rate 50 basis points to 3.25 percent, the last of four cuts in easing cycle which began on May 10 and accelerated in wake of September 11 attacks on U.S. Euro closes at $0.8926. \par \par \uc2  * Sept 17, 2002 - Euro rises to six-month highs of $0.9333 in the aftermath of the Sept 11 suicide attacks on U.S. cities. \par \par \uc2  * Sept 11, 2002 - Two hijacked planes hit twin towers of New York's World Trade Center. Euro rises two percent to $0.9169. \par \par \uc2  * July 31, 2001 - Euro falls to $0.8344, little more than one cent above record lows, suffering from poor perception of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy relative to that of the U.S. Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  * Jan 5, 2001 - Euro rises to nine-month highs of $0.9595, highs not surpassed until June 2002, as concerns mount over the state of the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  * Jan 3, 2001 - U.S. Federal Reserve cuts the federal funds rate 50 basis points to 6.0 percent. The move marks start of aggressive interest rate cuts which will last until December 2001, slashing rates to 1.75 percent in the course of the year. Euro closes at $0.9281. \par \par \uc2  * Nov 10, 6, 3, 2000 - ECB in conjunction with national euro zone central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros, leaving the euro trading around $0.86. \par \par \uc2  * Oct 26, 2000 - Euro hits record low of $0.8225, 30 percent below its launch value. \par \par \uc2  * Oct 16, 2000 - European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg tells London Times he "wouldn't think" it would make sense to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if war in the Middle East caused a sharp change in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Euro falls to $0.8455. \par \par \uc2  * Sept 22, 2000 - Central banks in Europe, Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , acting together for first time since 1995, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive euro higher after \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits low below $0.85 two days earlier. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is first by ECB since its birth. \par \par \uc2  * Aug 22, 2000 - German Ifo July business climate survey falls steeply to lowest in nine months. U.S. Fed leaves interest rates steady. Euro hits three-month low at $0.8940. \par \par \uc2  * July 28, 2000 - Strong U.S. second quarter growth data, up 5.2 percent, underscores market view that European growth is lagging. Euro closes at $0.9230. \par \par \uc2  * April 18, 2000 - Euro zone consumer price inflation for March rises to 2.1 percent, breaks above ECB's 2.0 percent ceiling. Euro closes at $0.9457. \par \par \uc2  * March 9, 2000 - ECB's monthly report warns of risk of rising inflation in euro area due in part to weaker euro. Euro closes at $0.9662. \par \par \uc2  * Dec 2, 1999 - European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg says euro has strong potential to appreciate. Euro falls to one-for-one with the dollar. \par \par \uc2  * Apr 8, 1999 - European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes first monetary policy move of its career, lowering key refinancing rate 50 basis points to 2.50 percent. Euro closes at $1.0798. \par \par \uc2  * March 15, 1999 - European Commission resigns en masse amid a financial mismanagement scandal. Euro closes at $1.0943. \par \par \uc2  * March 11, 1999 - German Finance Minister Oskar Lafontaine resigns. Euro at $1.1028. \par \par \uc2  * Jan 4, 1999 - Euro begins trading at $1.1747, hitting a high of $1.1906 on the same day. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020715dy7f00mq6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
