\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar slips on anthrax worries, trade thin. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Isabel Reynolds \par \uc2 761 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2001\par 08:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The dollar traded in a narrow range against the yen on Monday, weighed by fears over the spate of anthrax contamination cases in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  but supported by fear of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The anthrax cases in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  have become a talking point, and that is strengthening fears of retaliatory terrorist action," said one dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  Fears of biological assaults have been growing as U.S. officials said terrorists were likely behind the recent cases in which anthrax-contaminated mail had been sent to companies in Florida, New York and Nevada. \par \par \uc2  "Looked at very simply, these anthrax cases could constitute a second round of terrorist attacks, and that could mean U.S. military action will have to be more drawn out than previously thought," said Shuji Shirota, senior economist at Societe Generale Securities. \par \par \uc2  "By itself, that would be a negative for the dollar, but I don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will move on that factor alone," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-yen was bid around 121.00 after a thin day's trade, down from around 121.17 in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was bid at 91.27 cents compared with 91.13 cents in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also well-supported against the yen, trading at 110.44 yen from 110.42 yen, after dipping below 110 yen last week. \par \par \uc2  Making the most of the softer U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the Australian dollar, which spiked to one-month highs of around 51.40 cents from 50.20, before easing to 51.25. \par \par \uc2  The Aussie was helped by talk that diversified miner WMC Ltd was set for a break-up or takeover by Alcoa Inc, although there have been numerous rumours involving WMC in the past 18 months. \par \par \uc2  ANTHRAX SCARE \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders were left groping for direction after weak U.S. economic data and new anthrax cases knocked the dollar off a fresh one-month high of 121.74 on Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was recouping ground lost after the September 11 attacks. \par \par \uc2  News that U.S. retail sales fell 2.4 percent in September, the steepest falloff in nearly nine years, intensified worries that the U.S. economy was headed for recession. \par \par \uc2  "If the anthrax scare continues, then we may see additional damage to U.S. consumer spending, and that would be negative for the U.S. economy and the dollar," said Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  But despite the dollar's vulnerability, traders said it would remain supported against the yen as the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities remained. \par \par \uc2  Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven days late last month to halt an export-damaging rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "With the caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we are not going to see the dollar tumble to 119 or 118 yen," said SocGen's Shirota. \par \par \uc2  Many also doubted the dollar would see much damage as the yen struggled with problems of its own. \par \par \uc2  Data on Monday showed Japan's current account surplus shrank for the ninth straight month in August. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan also downgraded its view of the economy for a fifth straight month on worsening job and income conditions due to weaker production and on the negative impact of the attacks on the United States. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think we are going to see much good economic news either out of the U.S. or Japan in the near future. For new factors, we may need to look ahead to changes in monetary policy," Shirota said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0553 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls \par \par \uc2  12 Oct. \par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr              0.9125   0.9113   +0.13    -3.91   0.9496\par Dlr/yen               120.98   121.11   -0.11    +5.71   114.45\par Euro/yen              110.36   110.07   +0.26    +1.52   108.71\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par #VALUE!\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Stg/dlr               1.4528   1.4526   +0.01    -3.15   1.5000\par Can/dlr               1.5597   1.5625   -0.18    +4.58   1.4914\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par #VALUE!\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par #VALUE!\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/stg              0.6276   0.6272   +0.06    -0.77   0.6325.\par \par ..        Debt...      Indicators...\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots Tokyo spots Europe spots Volatilities Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from\par BOJ World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Official rates...\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par Press Digests....         