\par\par \b \uc2  Russian rouble slips, trade upset by U.S. woes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Artyom Danielyan \par \uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2001\par 13:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MOSCOW, Sept 13 (Reuters) - Russia suspended some \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade on Thursday due to settlement problems in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  following Tuesday's terror attacks while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support a slipping rouble. \par \par \uc2  Russia's main \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading venue, the Moscow Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange, (MICEX) said it had suspended afternoon trade. Dealers said problems also emerged earlier in the morning session when eight exchanges usually take part and set the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next-day official rate. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said no regional exchanges participated, only MICEX. The interbank market was trading normally. \par \par \uc2  "Due to technical problems at the Bank of New York , which is MICEX's settlement bank for the U.S. dollar, trade in U.S. dollar instruments will not be held on MICEX's 'afternoon' SELT session on September 13," MICEX said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. financial system has been hit since two hijacked planes on Tuesday rammed into the World Trade Centre, where many large banks, including the Bank of New York, are based. \par \par \uc2  In the afternoon session roubles are traded for today, tomorrow and spot settlement, although volumes are usually low. \par \par \uc2  The rouble's weighted average for today settlement in the morning session ticked down to 29.4696 roubles per dollar after 29.4455 per dollar the previous day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its official next-day at 29.47 after a previous 29.45 . \par \par \uc2  Russia's dollarised economy holds the second biggest amount of dollars in circulation after the United States. Banks and households, which have squirreled away an estimated $30 billion, are sensitive to any rouble/dollar hitches. \par \par \uc2  However, the atmosphere on the street was calm, with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange booths quoting normal buy and sell rates, rather than the slashed buy rate some posted on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  SLOW RUSSIA TRADE \par \par \uc2  Russian banks were too preoccupied with settlement problems to trade actively and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in morning trade and on the interbank market, being virtually the only supplier of dollars. \par \par \uc2  "Trade is very slow. Everyone is busy with current payments. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  satisfied all dollar demand in the morning trade because banks failed to deposit dollars," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Trade volume in the morning session was $66.72 million. \par \par \uc2  One dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told all large banks it would buy any sums directly from counteragents at the average morning session rate if banks failed to deposit funds for trade. \par \par \uc2  Regional exchange officials said MICEX cut them off from trade at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's request. They said they did not have a link with the Bank of New York, which gave details on the presence of dollars in trade participants' accounts via SWIFT. \par \par \uc2  On the interbank market, the rouble initially fell to 29.48-29.49 per dollar, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 29.47 roubles per dollar. Dealers said they expected a quiet market. \par \par \uc2  "There are no macroeconomic preconditions for a dollar rate change," a dealer said. "Tomorrow will be as quiet as today People will have to digest the situation and the United States has to put its payment system in order." \par \par \uc2  Metallinvestbank dealer Alexander Panasenko said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would smooth any sharp fluctuations, although banks themselves would avoid them due to the settlement difficulties. \par \par \uc2  Interbank roubles for tomorrow settlement were 29.4700/29.4800 versus Wednesday's last deal of 29.47. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010913dx9d00nmk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
