\par\par \b \uc2  Latvia lat firms 20 points amid dollar selling. \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2001\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  RIGA, Sept 12 (Reuters) - The Latvian lat firmed against the SDR basket in early Wednesday trading amid dollar selling following Tuesday's terror attacks in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and dealers said the lat could hit the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level later in the day. \par \par \uc2  At 0832 GMT the lat was 23 points off its top \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level - the strongest point it is allowed to reach in its two percent band against the SDR basket. It traded 43 points off the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level early on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone is selling (dollars), both cash and non-cash," Hansabanka \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Sandris Pavlovs said. \par \par \uc2  "I understand that clearing for yesterday's transactions has not taken place, and that could leave some impact on exchange rates and dollar could fall," he added. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the dollar recouped some losses against the euro it had sustained that level in the wake of Tuesday's attacks but trading was thin as the market was paralysed in the aftermath of the destraction of the World Trade Centre. \par \par \uc2  "I think the lat can rise to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. If it does happen it will happen today, it already rose 20 points in two hours," Pavlovs said. \par \par \uc2  The lat usually firms in its band against the SDR basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when there is dollar selling onthe local market. \par \par \uc2  On the local market, the dollar was 0.6187/91 against the lat, down from 0.6248/53 early on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was 0.6165/290, where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within its two percent band against the SDR. \par \par \uc2  The lat is pegged at 0.7997 to the IMF's world \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, the SDR - which includes the dollar, the yen and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It is allowed to fluctuate in a band of one percent either side. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engages in passive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it leaves that range. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx9c0111k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
