\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  problems seen taking back seat to growth at G7. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lida Poletz \par \uc2 801 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2001\par 12:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 4 (Reuters) - G7 finance ministers are unlikely to hammer out a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy when they meet in Rome on Saturday despite market speculation about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts say. \par \par \uc2  Sluggish global growth - and how to kick-start it - will take centre stage at the meeting of the Group of Seven major industrialised countries, while \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns will be relegated to the sidelines, they say. \par \par \uc2  This view was reinforced after a U.S. Treasury official said on Tuesday there were no plans for any special discussion of exchange rates at the G7 meeting and Haruhiko Kuroda, Japan' top financial diplomat, reiterated the point on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are part of the story, but the centerpiece is really growth," said Ram Bhagavatula, chief economist at Royal Bank of Scotland in New York. \par \par \uc2  "STRONG DOLLAR" PINCHES U.S. \par \par \uc2  With the euro dangling near record lows and recession-hit U.S. manufacturers bemoaning the dollar's strength, exchange rate imbalances have become a thorn in the side of policymakers on both sides of the Atlantic. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise this year to 15-year highs against a basket of its major trading partners' \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sparked vociferous complaints from U.S. manufacturers, who say their competitiveness overseas is being damaged. \par \par \uc2  But in the run-up to the G7 meeting, the U.S. Treasury has repeatedly insisted it will keep its inflation-busting "strong dollar" policy intact. \par \par \uc2  "A lot of companies were burned by the strong dollar, but the Treasury has implied that it's their internal issue - i.e. don't blame the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  adviser Bernard Tsui at Union Bank of California. \par \par \uc2  Rather than intentionally weaken the dollar to fuel exports, analysts say, Washington would prefer to see the euro zone and Japan pump up their economies by easing monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  "It's hard to imagine the U.S. is ready to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  misalignments at all," said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist James McCormick at J.P. Morgan Chase. \par \par \uc2  "The more pressing issue is that domestic demand in these two large regions, Europe and Japan, is quite weak - and the U.S. would like to see some policies put in place to support it." \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise has been boosted by global investors' expectations that a series of aggressive U.S. interest rate cuts this year will help turn around America's economic slowdown. \par \par \uc2  EUROPE AT A LOSS TO STEM EURO SLIDE \par \par \uc2  In Europe, meanwhile, officials are perceived to be loath to see the euro continue to decline, as its depreciation is viewed as psychologically damaging and also as it helps feed inflation. \par \par \uc2  Still, the weakness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is helping European exporters' competitiveness at a time when the region's economy is showing signs of slowing. \par \par \uc2  At any rate, the ECB has repeatedly dampened down expectations of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and may be resigned to living with a weak euro for the time being - especially if the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unwilling to help out with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "They're paying lip service to a strong euro, but privately they're acknowledging that the chances of it turning dramatically between now and when they introduce notes and coins (on January 1) is limited," said Standard Chartered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Tim Fox. \par \par \uc2  "So, I don't see them moving to force the issue in the period before the end of the year." \par \par \uc2  The euro is currently within three cents of its record lows set last October, and below levels at which the G7 countries - Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  - \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly on the eve of their September gathering to halt its persistent decline. \par \par \uc2  But the economic backdrop has changed dramatically since then. The U.S. economy has slowed dramatically, and euro zone economic growth has underperformed expectations. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Japan, is verging on recession and facing a dearth of policy options to rev up its economy. \par \par \uc2  The market still suspects that the Japanese may have to weaken the yen, but last weekend's U.S.-Japanese summit gave traders few clues about yen policy. The G7 may have little to add. \par \par \uc2  This week, Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi said he had no intention of consciously bringing the yen lower. \par \par \uc2  That's in line with the White House view that the U.S. will tolerate a softer yen if that weakening results from badly needed structural reforms, but that a deliberate yen depreciation would be unacceptable. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. administration's reluctance to tweak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy artificially suggests that the G7 is unlikely to issue any kind of explicit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  If anything, the G7 may repeat what it said at its previous meeting in April, that exchange rates should "reflect economic fundamentals". \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx74007jd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
