\par\par \b \uc2  Euro drop in 2000 was normal dip - Fed's Poole. \b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 13:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WASHINGTON, March 27 (Reuters) - The euro's weakness against the dollar last year was a "perfectly normal" dip of a sort which all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  suffer from time to time, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis President William Poole said on Tuesday \par \par \uc2  Poole also said in a speech in Prague that higher growth in Europe depended on microeconomic reforms and not simply an expansionary monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  "There was a certain amount of anguish last year as the euro depreciated against the dollar, but that happens from time to time to the very best \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world," Poole said in remarks prepared for delivery to the European Banking and Financial Forum. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar, of course, has seen its ups and downs over the years," he said in an upbeat assessment of the euro, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's effectiveness and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's potential impact on Europe's economy. \par \par \uc2  "That the euro was beset by nothing more serious than a perfectly normal period of weakness is evidence of just how remarkable the achievement (creation of the euro) has been." \par \par \uc2  The euro was officially launched on January 1, 1999, as a common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for European countries, but sank in 2000 despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from countries around the world, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It started last year at $1.0050, but fell to $0.8225 on October 26 before making a partial recovery. It was just below $0.90 as Poole spoke. \par \par \uc2  Its gains have been limited due in part to falling stock prices, which have led investors to buy U.S. dollars, considered a more stable investment. \par \par \uc2  Poole said the establishment of the euro will likely have many positive effects, including improving trade efficiency and unifying capital markets. But he said time will tell if the euro succeeds and he noted that single unified \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not cure-alls for all countries. \par \par \uc2  ECB DOING "EXCELLENT JOB" \par \par \uc2  Poole said the ECB has done an "excellent job" in establishing itself and its policies. \par \par \uc2  "The way in which the ECB handles the problems and even crises that will inevitably arise will shape future events," he said. "Every action by the ECB needs to be viewed as part of a developing long-term policy strategy and not just in terms of the pressures of the day." \par \par \uc2  The ECB is under pressure to cut its 4.75 percent minimum bid rate when it meets on Thursday. It is the only major \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has not cut rates this year in response to a slowdown in economies around the globe. \par \par \uc2  The St. Louis Fed chief, who is a voting member this year on the Federal Reserve's policymaking committee, also said the performance of the European economy is not entirely in the hands of the ECB. \par \par \uc2  "It is critical to understand that higher growth in Europe does not depend on an expansionary monetary policy, but instead on microeconomic reforms," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Good monetary policy contributes enormously to economic growth by creating price stability, but cannot be expected to create the microeconomic efficiencies that are at the heart of the growth process." \par \par \uc2  On the microeconomic side, Poole said Europe needs to increase flexibility in its labor markets, boost entrepreneurship and alter government oversight and tax policies to better encourage growth. \par \par \uc2  "The United States, although in better shape on many of the microeconomic dimensions than Europe, needs exactly the same reforms to increase its growth rate," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3r0399s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
