\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-ECB not getting enough credit for  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2000\par 17:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 23 (Reuters) - The reason the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers don't see eye to eye about the success of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro is because they use different yardsticks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have tended to judge the ECB's euro-buying sprees by how long the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds onto its gains. Therefore they have been swift to brand the euro's retreat from these peaks as a sign of failure. \par \par \uc2  But ECB President Wim Duisenberg said on Thursday it was too early to judge the success of the four forays the ECB has made into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the past two months. \par \par \uc2  He also said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at breaking an entrenched philosophy which viewed the euro as a one-way bet rather than to achieve a specific exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that on that basis the ECB could claim a good measure of success as its actions had introduced a degreee of wariness into a market which, until two months ago, had been confident it could drive the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ever lower. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB has definitely introduced two-way risk and has therefore done what it wanted to," said Peter von Maydell, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston in London. \par \par \uc2  "It is being criticised for not getting the euro higher, but it is not its job to spend money in order to give the market a one-way bet on the upside." \par \par \uc2  EURO BEARS GET JUMPY \par \par \uc2  The ECB spearheaded euro-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Group of Seven industrial nations on September 22 and has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three more times since. \par \par \uc2  Joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan, Germany, France, Britain, Italy, and Canada drove the euro above $0.90 and kept it away from record lows for nearly a month. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sagged to new record lows by the end of October after Duisenberg said in a newspaper interview that the G7 would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if a crisis in the Middle East caused a sharp fall in its value. \par \par \uc2  Traders read the comments as a sign that more joint G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not on the cards and seized on the opportunity to beat the euro down as far as $0.8225, about 30 percent below levels it was launched at in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  But while the G7 has not made another joint appearance on the foreign exchanges, the ECB has shown itself willing to take action on its own by making three solo \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in November. \par \par \uc2  This allowed the euro to stage one of its most enduring rallies in more than a year against the dollar earlier this month. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since slipped back, but even the suspicion that the ECB may be lurking in the wings is now enough to get traders scrambling to buy euros - a far cry from pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  days when euro bears had no fears. \par \par \uc2  "The euro may have ceded a bit of ground but the ECB has managed to break that one-way market by making it clear that there is risk attached to being short of the euro," said Mike Lenhoff, portfolio strategist at Capel-Cure Sharp in London. \par \par \uc2  He said his institution was slightly overweight of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that it intended to hold onto that position. \par \par \uc2  IS ECB LINE A GET-OUT CLAUSE? \par \par \uc2  To be sure, international policymakers have made it clear they would prefer to see the euro higher. \par \par \uc2  The G7 said after they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the euro's protracted weakness posed a potential threat to the world economy. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Duisenberg said on Thursday the euro's losses represented an overshooting and that policymakers firmly believed the move would be reversed. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said it was no surprise that the ECB was stressing that the goal of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not specifically to achieve this reversal. \par \par \uc2  "If the euro hits new record lows, it will be hard to say the ECB's reputation has been damaged, given that all they say they are trying to do is to introduce two-way risk," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg in London. \par \par \uc2  "It is a good get-out clause." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbn00ve0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
