\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar gets lift, pound suffers on US holiday. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2000\par 01:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 23 (Reuters) - The dollar approached recent nine-month highs against the yen and rose to three-week peaks against the euro on Thursday, as European traders nudged the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher over the U.S. Thanksgiving holiday. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's biggest gains came against a broadly weaker sterling. \par \par \uc2  Growing expectations that British rates have peaked drove the pound to two-month lows below $1.40 - within half a cent of 14-year lows set in September. Sterling also hit one-week lows against the euro. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the broad trend for the dollar was for further strength, and only holidays in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Japan and wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro were preventing the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from gaining more ground. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is still well-supported," said Teis Knuthsen, chief strategist at SEB Merchant Banking in Copenhagen. \par \par \uc2  "A weekly close above 110 could move the dollar into the mid-teens against the yen." \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose as high as 110.38 , according to Reuters data, a touch below nine-month highs of 110.43 set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Political uncertainty in Japan and the U.S. dollar's resilience to the ongoing U.S. election saga were likely to catapault the dollar out of ranges against the yen which have confined it for much of this year, analysts and dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the economic outlook in the euro zone suggested only further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hold the euro above $0.84, and it fell below the three-week lows set on Wednesday, they added. \par \par \uc2  The ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times this month in an attempt to counteract euro weakness triggered by relative pessimism about the euro zone economic outlook compared with the United States. \par \par \uc2  The $0.85 level is now widely regarded as the ECB's threshold of tolerance for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts and traders said, although ECB President Wim Duisenberg reiterated on Thursday that it did not have an exchange rate target. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $0.8404/07 at 1614 GMT. The euro set a record low of $0.8225 late last month, before the ECB started its solo \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  MARKET TAKES LITTLE NOTE OF DUISENBERG \par \par \uc2  Comments from Duisenberg had limited impact in holiday-thinned trade, analysts and traders said. Duisenberg said it was far too early to make a judgement about the effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mainly used to break a prevailing philosophy in the markets and introduce two-way risk. He also said the euro's losses reflected an overshooting which the ECB did not like. \par \par \uc2  ECB executive board member Jean-Claude Trichet, meanwhile, recommended caution on consensus euro-zone growth forecasts, saying growth could vary this year and next. \par \par \uc2  The latest picture on continuing strong German inflation became clearer, with the release of November consumer price data from the states of Bavaria and North Rhine-Westphalia, which both showed year-on-year rises of 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  This followed consumer price inflation of 2.4 percent reported on Wednesday by the states of Hesse and Baden-Wuerttemberg. \par \par \uc2  "The data were a little bit stronger than expected, which may keep alive expectations that the ECB will have to tighten monetary policy sooner than others," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One in London. \par \par \uc2  In a largely rangebound session, sterling's slide to two-month lows against the dollar and one-week lows against the euro caught traders' attention. \par \par \uc2  Sterling fell below $1.40 to half a cent above 14-year lows around $1.3945 hit in September. It also fell to one-week lows beyond 60.20 pence per euro. \par \par \uc2  "Sterling is in a well-defined downtrend against the dollar and is testing support levels that go back to the ERM crisis in 1992," said Neil Mackinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch in London. \par \par \uc2  Mackinnon added that sterling remained vulnerable to the downside and could fall as low as $1.35 on a one-to three-month time horizon. \par \par \uc2  Data on Thursday showed Britain's economy grew an unrevised 0.7 percent in the third quarter, leaving output 2.9 percent higher than a year earlier. \par \par \uc2  The Confederation of British Industry on Thursday forecast British interest rates to stay at 6.0 percent until the end of 2001, and to fall to 5.5 percent in the second half of 2002. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar held clear of record lows around US$0.5070 set against the U.S. dollar a day ago, amid talk the Reserve Bank of Australia may have been buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the European morning session around US$0.5215. \par \par \uc2  It rebounded from its all-time troughs later on Wednesday to stage to its sharpest one-day rally in more than two years. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar slackened off by late European trade, quoted near the day's lows around US$0.5200 , from earlier two-week highs near US$0.53. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwbn0bbyg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
