\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro steady, paralysed by ECB wariness, US vote. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Shinichi Kishima \par \uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2000\par 12:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 14 (Reuters) - The euro was steady against the dollar on Tuesday on wariness that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's support and on continued legal wrangling over last week's U.S. presidential election. \par \par \uc2  Traders were particularly mindful of the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as officials from the Group of Seven industrial nations met in Paris and after comments from Bank of England Governor Eddie George late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Speaking after a meeting of G10 central bankers in Mexico, George said he could not exclude the chance of further concerted G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though he added the caveat: "I don't know that that is imminent." \par \par \uc2  "Although it (George's remark) doesn't raise the spectre of immediate \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the G7 meeting today it's obviously going to fuel debate about whether there will be further G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ryan Shea, international economist at Bank One in London. \par \par \uc2  Speculation was rife that the G7 could discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even though their main agenda was aid for the Balkans. Dealers were all the more wary as joint G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro's support on September 22 came a day before a G7 meeting. \par \par \uc2  Even prospects of unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB was enough to keep traders cautious, given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made three such solo forays into the market in the past two weeks, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB has shown it is willing to come in at any time to stem the euro's decline," said Tamiko Bayliss, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \uc2  "There is still a huge appetite for dollars despite political confusion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  means traders are reluctant to drive the euro lower." \par \par \uc2  At 1051 GMT, the euro was trading at around $0.8590 EUR=), virtually unchanged from late Monday levels. It was also little changed against the yen at around 93.65 yen EURJPY=). \par \par \uc2  The euro barely moved after both the average and lowest rates in the ECB's weekly money market tender fell from a week earlier toward the ECB's minimum rate of 4.75 percent, given most market-watchers did not expect the ECB to raise interest rates at Thursday's regular policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  U.S. POLITICAL SAGA DRAGS ON \par \par \uc2  Barring \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets would be driven by the twists and turns of the unfolding U.S. presidential drama. \par \par \uc2  Imposition of a Tuesday deadline for vote recounting in Florida appeared to favour Republican George W. Bush, but this deadline was challenged in the courts, with a decision due around 1530 GMT on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts assumed that if a full manual count were to be allowed, it would tend to favour Democrat Al Gore. \par \par \uc2  Bush was generally considered as less likely to support G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  than Gore, which is why the euro has tended to slip whenever events in the election have swung his way. \par \par \uc2  The political situation in Japan, meanwhile, was also fast descending into chaos, though the yen's losses were limited. \par \par \uc2  Embattled Prime Minister Yoshiro Mori defied calls for him to step aside but his main challenger, Koichi Kato, showed no signs of backing down and the opposition pressed ahead with plans for a no-confidence vote. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they saw longer term benefits if the deeply unpopular Mori was replaced by a more reformist leader. \par \par \uc2  "The political issue could drag the yen lower short term, but we have to see the next step. The next step might be a new prime minister who is better than the present one, which would be yen positive," said Karl Broeker, head of Treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttenburg. \par \par \uc2  The yen was about a quarter percent off from late Monday levels at around 107.85 to the dollar JPY=). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwbe025j6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
