\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-ECB digs in for protracted fight over euro. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lida Poletz \par \uc2 697 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2000\par 21:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Nov 9 (Reuters) - Europe's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fired off a new round of ammunition on Thursday to rescue its embattled euro, but analysts said it may be in for a long, lonely war of attrition against a stubbornly bearish market. \par \par \uc2  In its third \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in five trading days, the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) bought euros against both the dollar and yen, shaking the market out of a torpor caused by the uncertainty over the U.S. presidential election. \par \par \uc2  "Clearly they're trying to bring some stability to the euro and show that they're serious," said Jay Bryson, global economist at First Union National Bank in Charlotte, N.C. "If they keep coming in every few days, they'll show that they're willing to do what it takes to bring stability to the euro." \par \par \uc2  But after leaping over half a cent and a full yen, the euro drifted off its highs, repeating a pattern established in earlier ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday and Monday. \par \par \uc2  The quick climbdown indicates the market is in no hurry to end it euro-selling trend, analysts said, although the euro later bounced back against a dollar suffering from mounting election confusion. \par \par \uc2  "Our view going forward is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not succeed in improving the tone of the euro unless there is further evidence of a change in the economic fundamentals," said Chris Widness, international economist at Chase Securities in New York. \par \par \uc2  BUILDING A BASE \par \par \uc2  Judging by the ECB's three solo \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to date, it appears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not aiming to push the euro significantly higher, but simply to build a base and keep it from retesting record lows, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "ECB officials have made it clear that the objective of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not to push the euro to some predetermined level against the dollar, but to underscore its belief that the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was undervalued," said Marc Chandler, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Mellon Bank. \par \par \uc2  Six weeks ago, the ECB was joined in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the Group of Seven wealthy countries in a rare joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the euro. But the euro quickly resumed its downward slide, hitting record lows near 82.25 cents and 89 yen last month before rebounding. \par \par \uc2  In afternoon trade on Thursday, the euro was changing hands at around 86.60 cents and 93 yen. \par \par \uc2  Repetition looks to be the key of the pattern developing in the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  - buying euros in small batches and trying to take advantage of significant technical levels, said analysts. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB seems to be determined to maintain the euro above 85 cents and is taking advantage of the uncertainty which reigns in the market, as we still do not know the outcome of the U.S. elections," said Fabio Fraschetti, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banca Nazionale del Lavorno in London. \par \par \uc2  "They are trying to make the market tired by continuing to support the euro/dollar," Fraschetti said. \par \par \uc2  U.S. ELECTION ADDS TWIST \par \par \uc2  Six weeks ago, when the ECB launched its first euro buying spree, it was joined by G7 countries in a dramatic, joint \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  that made euro bears think twice about aggressively selling the euro - at least temporarily. \par \par \uc2  But since then, significantly, the G7 partners outside the euro zone - the United States, Japan, Britain and Canada - have kept their distance. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' hands-off approach during the three most recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bouts is sure to continue as long as the outcome of Tuesday's presidential election remains uncertain, leaving the ECB to continue fending for itself analysts said. \par \par \uc2  In the latest twist to the election drama, Democrat Al Gore decided to fight the results of the election in Florida, which showed Republican candidate George W. Bush with a slim lead. \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, protracted election uncertainty could actually help the euro, some analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "This might be the best bit of timing because I'm negative on the election process and what it means for the dollar, even if it is resolved in the next couple of days," said David Gilmore, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb902f9q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
