\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro mired against dollar, eyes U.S. election result. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sabrina Ghani \par \uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2000\par 12:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 9 (Reuters) - The euro was mired near recent one-week lows against the dollar on Thursday as dealers waited for the result of a recount in the state of Florida which will determine who will be the next president of the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, persistent wariness of renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acted unilaterally in defence of the euro last Friday and on Monday, was preventing aggressive selling of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market is very much in a sell euro mode, although the possibility of further ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slowing the euro's decline," said a trader at a Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "We have the U.S. election confirmation later today and it looks like Bush is going to win. That would give the euro another shunt lower against the dollar." \par \par \uc2  This gridlock meant one of the biggest movers was the broadly weaker pound, which hit seven-week lows against the dollar, amid expectations the Bank of England Monetary Policy Committee would leave interest rates unchanged later on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown's pre-budget statement on Wednesday, while generous, did not change expectations rates would be left at 6.0 percent on Thursday given recent signs the economy was slowing, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  BUSH WIN SEEN BETTER FOR DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The recount in Florida is expected to be completed at around 2200 GMT but the dollar's firmness suggested traders were betting on a victory by Republican George W. Bush. \par \par \uc2  But if absentee ballots mailed in from overseas were needed to determine the outcome, it could take until those ballots are counted on November 17 for the results to be finalised. \par \par \uc2  Traders expected the euro to lose further ground if Bush won the election as the Republican administration was seen promoting a looser and more business-friendly fiscal policy. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, Bush's administration was seen less likely to support joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in defence of the euro, they added. \par \par \uc2  The euro was pinned within half a cent of one-week lows around $0.8515 it had set on Wednesday after U.S. television networks projected Bush had won the election. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the euro could get a lift if Florida overturned earlier projections and Democratic candidate Al Gore won the presidency later in the day. \par \par \uc2  The euro retained a soft tone against the yen, hovering just above Wednesday's one-week lows around 91.40 yen, although was getting some reprieve from wariness of more euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB. \par \par \uc2  The Group of Seven industrial nations jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop the euro on September 22 and the ECB conducted unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help the euro last Friday and on Monday. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts said recent comments by European policy-makers were confusing the market over the ultimate objective of the ECB's market action. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, ECB Chief Economist Otmar Issing said the latest ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a success and was upbeat on the euro zone's economic outlook despite recent soft data. \par \par \uc2  "This is not a helpful comment. It suggests the ECB's objectives were not great given that the euro is one big figure below the levels it was at before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ian Gunner, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO in London. \par \par \uc2  "Maybe their objective is to reduce the weakness of the euro rather than to instigate the recovery." \par \par \uc2  On the other hand Bundesbank's President Ernst Welteke was quoted on Wednesday as saying the euro was 25 to 30 percent undervalued against the dollar and that he was concerned about its persistent weakness. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, dollar/yen was largely sidelined, continuing within the boundaries of this week's narrow range below Wednesday's one-week highs around 107.85 yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb902dmj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
