\par\par \b \uc2  NY Fed calls G7 euro  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  "successful". \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lida Poletz \par \uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2000\par 22:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Nov 8 (Reuters) - The Federal Reserve Bank of New York said on Wednesday the Group of Seven was successful in halting the euro's September slump in a joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  six weeks ago but was mum about future U.S. action in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  In a rare move, U.S. monetary authorities had joined the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) and other G7 wealthy nations on Sept. 22 to shore up Europe's ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying euros while selling dollars and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The United States spent $1.34 billion to buy 1.5 billion euros, the Fed said in its quarterly report to Congress. The figures were line with earlier market estimates. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  was successful in terms of what you expect from an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Peter Fischer, executive vice president of the New York Fed. "It broke the psychology of the one-way market, which is the first and best thing you can expect from an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  He told a news briefing the action to restore some stability to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was not at odds with the U.S. Treasury's long-standing policy in favor a strong dollar. \par \par \uc2  The report said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  had begun at 7:11 a.m. (1111 GMT) on Sept. 22, when the euro was trading at 87.50 cents against the dollar, and the Fed's trading desk traded intermittently until 9:20 a.m. (1320 GMT). \par \par \uc2  NO CLUES ON FURTHER \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Fischer gave no hint on whether U.S. participation was a one-time move or whether the market could expect further joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  The day of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro rallied nearly 3 cents to highs above 90 cents, but since then has fallen off, and two subsequent solo forays into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the ECB this month have failed to give the euro a lasting boost. \par \par \uc2  In U.S. trade on Wednesday the dollar stood at 85.40 cents, well below the G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highs. \par \par \uc2  The G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had followed a sharp increase in market volatility in early September, prompted by reports of capital outflows from the euro area and repositioning by Japanese firms, the Fed report said. \par \par \uc2  "The euro began to trade in a one-way market," Fischer said. "The euro's movement downward began to accelerate as a self-fulfilling prophecy, and in that environment and on the initiative of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  joined Group of Seven monetary authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The euro fell 2.8 percent against the yen and 1.9 percent against the dollar in the first week of September, while option implied volatility for the euro surged, the report said. \par \par \uc2  Fischer said U.S. monetary authorities were not targeting any specific levels for the dollar against the euro. \par \par \uc2  "Levels matter to traders, and we are speaking to the trading community when we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But to us, the market dynamic is more important than levels," Fischer said. \par \par \uc2  "STRONG DOLLAR" POLICY INTACT \par \par \uc2  The Fed report noted that Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers had restated that a strong dollar is in the national interest, even as the United States joined the G7 to boost the euro against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Fischer said former Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin had reiterated the same "strong dollar" policy in 1998, when the United States had sold dollars and bought yen when the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was weakening sharply. \par \par \uc2  "Even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the direction of our allies' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in the long run the strong dollar policy is in the strategic interest of the United States," Fischer said. \par \par \uc2  Rubin and Summers had repeatedly said a strong dollar is good for the country because it keeps inflation and interest rates in check. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREIGN EXCHANGE\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES \par \par \uc2  The Fed said the dollar had appreciated 8.2 percent against the euro and 2.0 percent against the yen in the third quarter, and ended the quarter 4.1 percent stronger against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the United States' major trading partners. \par \par \uc2  The foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  holdings of U.S. monetary authorities, based on current exchange levels, rose slightly, reflecting the increase from the euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , minus the valuation adjustments caused by the dollar's gains during that period. \par \par \uc2  The total holdings of euro and yen totaled $31.2 billion as of Sept. 29, compared to $31.0 billion the previous quarter, excluding interest receivables. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb802g8n\par }\page {\par\fs20{