\par\par \b \uc2  Euro easier, market eyes further  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2      By Masayuki Kitano \par \uc2 935 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2000\par 06:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      TOKYO, Nov 6 (Reuters) - The euro was easier in late \par \par \uc2  afternoon on Monday as last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) failed to deter selling by Japanese exporters, \par \par \uc2  although wariness of more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action lent some support. \par \par \uc2      The euro was quoted at $0.8656/61 against $0.8664 in late \par \par \uc2  U.S. trading on Friday. \par \par \uc2      The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 92.80/85 yen as of 0513 \par \par \uc2  GMT, up from 92.60 yen in late U.S. trading on Friday, but a long \par \par \uc2  way off its post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  peak above 95 yen. \par \par \uc2      It was initially pressured against the yen due to selling by \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters, but reclaimed some ground as dealers sold yen \par \par \uc2  against the dollar. \par \par \uc2      "The dollar's failure to break below 107 yen spurred some buy \par \par \uc2  backs of dollars against yen by dealers looking to cut losses," \par \par \uc2  said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2      The greenback's modest rise against the yen also indirectly \par \par \uc2  helped the euro against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dealer said. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the yen got little encouragement from a three \par \par \uc2  percent rise in the key Nikkei 225 stocks average, saying the \par \par \uc2  outlook for equity markets was too opaque for sentiment to change \par \par \uc2  dramatically based on a day's gains. \par \par \uc2      The dollar stood at 107.14/17 yen against 107.01 yen in late \par \par \uc2  U.S. trading on Friday. \par \par \uc2      In the near term, dealers said they would focus on whether \par \par \uc2  the ECB would take more euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves after \par \par \uc2  Friday's action. \par \par \uc2      A meeting of euro zone finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  governors in Brussels later on Monday was likely to be a source \par \par \uc2  of verbal support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      But dealers said the euro was likely to languish unless more \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place. \par \par \uc2      "The supply and demand balance continues to weigh against the \par \par \uc2  euro. There are a lot of traders who are looking to sell the euro \par \par \uc2  on rallies," said the city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2      Indeed, dealers said they detected sporadic euro-selling by \par \par \uc2  Japanese exporters in the morning. \par \par \uc2      "We've seen exporters selling the euro today. The euro's rise \par \par \uc2  to around 95 yen right after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday provided \par \par \uc2  them with a good opportunity to sell, and they still have a lot \par \par \uc2  more positions to sell," said a U.S. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Market players said that, although Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took \par \par \uc2  them by surprise, its impact was limited because it was not a \par \par \uc2  coordinated action with other Group of Seven (G7) industrialised \par \par \uc2  countries. \par \par \uc2      But they added the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought home the risks of \par \par \uc2  speculative selling of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      "Last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed us it is difficult to get \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  involved in market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it also \par \par \uc2  showed the ECB will act alone," said the U.S. dealer. \par \par \uc2      The market is wary of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB and \par \par \uc2  some speculated the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may help out. \par \par \uc2      Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs \par \par \uc2  Haruhiko Kuroda said on Monday the ECB acted appropriately when \par \par \uc2  it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the beleaguered euro on Friday. \par \par \uc2      "The euro was too weak against the yen and the dollar. The \par \par \uc2  ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was natural and in line with the G7 statement \par \par \uc2  in September," Kuroda told reporters. \par \par \uc2      In September, the G7 said they shared concern about the \par \par \uc2  potential implications of falls in the euro for the world's \par \par \uc2  economy. \par \par \uc2      Many dealers expect the dollar-yen rate to hold steady before \par \par \uc2  the U.S. presidential election on Tuesday. Traders said the large \par \par \uc2  tax cuts proposed by Republican candidate George W. Bush would \par \par \uc2  likely lead to higher U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  With the race still widely considered too close to call, most \par \par \uc2  in the market are hesitant to move before the election results \par \par \uc2  are in, they said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0546 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab    03 Nov.\par \tab \tab -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr   0.8659   0.8664   -0.06   -14.01   1.0070\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/yen    107.23   107.01   +0.21    +4.91   102.21\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    92.81    92.60   +0.23    -9.98   103.10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss  1.7545   1.7532   +0.07   +10.33   1.5902\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Stg/dlr    1.4473   1.4485   -0.08   -10.53   1.6176\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Can/dlr    1.5309   1.5321   -0.08    +5.91   1.4455\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Aus/dlr    0.5277   0.5259   +0.34   -19.59   0.6563\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/swiss 1.5192   1.5207   -0.10    -5.26   1.6036\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/stg   0.5982   0.5978   +0.07    -4.12   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0546 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   03 Nov.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8659   0.8664   -0.06   -14.01   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    107.23   107.01   +0.21    +4.91   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    92.81    92.60   +0.23    -9.98   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7545   1.7532   +0.07   +10.33   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4473   1.4485   -0.08   -10.53   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.5309   1.5321   -0.08    +5.91   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5277   0.5259   +0.34   -19.59   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5192   1.5207   -0.10    -5.26   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.5