\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro under pressure, but wary of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 626 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2000\par 04:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 6 (Reuters) - The euro remained under pressure on Monday as last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) failed to deter selling by Japanese exporters, although wariness of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  lent support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We've seen exporters selling in the euro today. The euro's rise to round 95 yen right after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday provided them with a good opportunity to sell, and they still have a lot more positions to sell," said a U.S. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  At the Tokyo midday the euro was quoted at $0.8653/58. Against the yen it was around 92.64/74 yen . \par \par \uc2  Market players said that, although Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took them by surprise, its impact was limited because it was not a coordinated action with other Group of seven (G7) industrialised countries. \par \par \uc2  But they added the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  brought home the risks of speculative selling of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed us it is difficult to get the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  involved in market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But it also showed the ECB will act alone, even without American cooperation," said the U.S. dealer. \par \par \uc2  The market is wary of another wave of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the ECB and some speculate the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might lend a helping hand. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda said on Monday the ECB acted appropriately when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to prop up the beleaguered euro. \par \par \uc2  "The euro was too weak against the yen and the dollar. The ECB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was natural and in line with the G7 statement in September," Kuroda told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The yen eased slightly to 107.11/21 yen against the dollar on Monday morning after Japanese importers bought the greenback, although it retained most of its post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains. \par \par \uc2  Before the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the yen was trading around 108 to the dollar. The yen's subsequent jump against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in part reflected robust selling of euros for yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although some traders said a slowing down in the U.S. economy is also hurting the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The last time the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market (on Sept 22), the yen fell against the dollar. This time it went in the opposite direction. Probably the market is now more nervous about the U.S. economy," said the U.S. bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers expect the dollar/yen rate to hold steady before the U.S. presidential election on Tuesday. Traders said the large tax-cuts proposed by Republic candidate George W. Bush would likely lead to higher U.S. interest rates. \par \par \uc2  With the race still widely considered too close to call, most players are hesitant to move before the election results are in, they said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0244 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab     Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   03 Nov.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8654   0.8664   -0.12   -14.06   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    107.05   107.01   +0.04    +4.74   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    92.64    92.60   +0.04   -10.15   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7558   1.7532   +0.15   +10.41   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4476   1.4485   -0.06   -10.51   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.5314   1.5321   -0.05    +5.94   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5265   0.5259   +0.11   -19.78   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5198   1.5207   -0.06    -5.23   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.5974   0.5978   -0.07    -4.25   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb602mfm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
