\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-ECB seizes golden opportunity with solo  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  stand. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 874 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2000\par 17:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 3 (Reuters) - Opportunism, rather than bravery, may have impelled the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to launch its first solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the foreign exchanges but the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands to benefit regardless. \par \par \uc2  The ECB went on a euro-buying spree on Friday which capitalised on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most enduring rally in a year and signs that financial markets' five-year love affair with the dollar could be drawing to a close amid slowing U.S. growth. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted the euro more than 1.5 cents against the dollar and could have sent it even higher and for longer if it had been joined by other Group of Seven industrial nations, as was the case less than two months ago. \par \par \uc2  But U.S. backing was seen elusive so close to Tuesday's presidential elections - a view which was reinforced after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke said it was difficult for the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to join \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this time. \par \par \uc2  And with no guarantee the U.S. would join \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the elections, particularly if Republican George W. Bush won, the ECB did well to seize a golden opportunity to put the euro on a stronger footing, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "I suspect they had difficulty persuading the U.S. to come in given the elections are coming up, but it was a wonderful backdrop against which to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Johnathan Bayley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Paribas in Paris. \par \par \uc2  "The euro had put in a solid week of rallies and both sentiment and data were going their way so the ECB were absolutely right to do it." \par \par \uc2  NO LINE IN SAND TO DEFEND? \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the ECB's decision to keep its powder dry until the euro was already rallying rather than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week when the euro was plumbing record lows near $0.8225 showed it had not set itself a specific exchange rate to defend. \par \par \uc2  Instead, the ECB was seen more concerned with successfully engineering a broader reversal in sentiment towards the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had lost as much as 30 percent of its value against the dollar since its January 1999 launch. \par \par \uc2  "We have already seen that they are clearly not preoccupied by any particular level," said Graham Cocks, manager, corporate treasury at Mellon Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "It looks rather as if they wanted to underpin the slightly more positive tone underlying the euro recently." \par \par \uc2  Central banks have typically found the cheapest way of getting what they want when it comes to exchange rates is to work with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets rather than fighting them. \par \par \uc2  And given the ECB knew it would be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone, it was likely keen to have as much going in its favour as it could, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  European central bankers earlier this year flagged the risks of solo action, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro's support would not work without U.S. and Japanese aid. \par \par \uc2  This view was backed by an ECB research paper published in February which found that central banks were more successful in influencing exchange rates when authorities acted in concert and relatively infrequently. \par \par \uc2  September's G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  succeeded in keeping the euro away from record lows for nearly a month, and its subsequent swoon only came after off-the-cuff remarks by ECB President Wim Duisenberg got \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders thinking there was no more joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  planned soon. \par \par \uc2  But with the euro already having bounced about five percent away from record lows against the dollar, the ECB had a better chance of seeing its solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  succeed. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is falling may need coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is already rising does not," said Nick Parsons, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Commerzbank in London. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said they may have decided to show their support for the euro when the going was good given there was a question mark about U.S. backing for more joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While the looming presidential election was seen as the key reason why the U.S. Treasury would not want to get involved in another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Duisenberg's comments may not have helped either, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB has done a few things which have been detrimental to the euro subsequent to the last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Bayley at Paribas. \par \par \uc2  But that does not mean the U.S. was opposed to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  shared the ECB's concern about the euro. \par \par \uc2  Also, the ECB said on Friday that while its action was unilateral, it was in line with a statement the G7 issued after September's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The world's most powerful nations have said the euro's weakness poses a potential threat to the world economy, a formula which the ECB repeated on Friday. They also said in September they would keep cooperating as needed. \par \par \uc2  But by making a stand and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own, the ECB showed it was not always going to be reliant on other members of the G7 when it came to defending its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "They are coming out of the shadows and want to be seen as a force in their own right," said Parsons at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb302uey\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
