\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dented dollar braces for NAPM report. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Maggie Lake \par \uc2 513 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2000\par 16:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Nov 1 (Reuters) - The dollar was weaker across the board in early U.S. trade on Wednesday as dealers waited to see whether October's National Association of Purchasing Management's (NAPM) manufacturing survey would provide further evidence that the robust U.S. economy is finally slowing. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Tuesday showed a fall in manufacturing activity in the Chicago area and U.S. consumer confidence at its lowest level in a year, fuelling speculation that Europe may finally be closing the gap on U.S. growth. \par \par \uc2  "The euro gains are a result of the market's increased questions about U.S. relative performance compared to Europe," said Alex Beuzelin, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst at Ruesch International. "Anything to suggest the gap has narrowed or closed is going to be euro supportive." \par \par \uc2  Analysts polled by Reuters expect a 49.8 reading in the October NAPM, compared to a 49.9 reading in September. Any number below 50 is a sign of contraction. \par \par \uc2  The euro, benefiting from narrowing growth prospects, climbed to two-week peaks above 85.50 cents , more than three cents above the record low it hit last week. \par \par \uc2  It eased slightly in early U.S. dealings as traders gently tested the market's buying interest, but was still a half a percent higher than Tuesday's closing level. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen , the euro drifted off two-week highs hit overnight around 92.90. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also lost ground against the yen, trading down half a percent from the previous close, near 108.45 . \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit was also down over a half a percent versus the Swiss franc . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  THREAT LINGERS \par \par \uc2  Thin volumes due to public holidays in many European countries was limiting the action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday, but traders remained on guard for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains, especially at the moment, given the euro's mini-uptrend and the fact that turnover is thin, which would exacerbate the move," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez in London. \par \par \uc2  Wariness of further euro-buying by central banks was rife after Bundesbank President Ernst Welteke and U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers both hinted at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they did not expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to join in any coordinated euro-buying spree just a week before the U.S. presidential elections, but added there was a greater chance the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Bank of Japan may decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by themselves. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, sterling tumbled to new two-week lows beyond 59 pence against the euro after a weaker-than-expected British manufacturing sector survey prompted a downward revision to UK interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The British headline purchasing managers index for October fell below the boom-or-bust 50 level for the first time in 18-months. \par \par \uc2  The Confederation of British Industry, meanwhile, reported its retail sales volume balance for October fell to zero from +14, its worst showing since January, 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwb102xh1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
