AUG 39  9     8   10  5    8     4    4    2     5     6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par AVG APR 45  8     6   12  3    8     8    3    0     3     2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab   U.S. Domestic Bond Allocations\par \tab \tab \tab -------------------------------\par \tab   TREAS    CORP    MORTGAGE    AGENCY   CASH   OTHR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2000-----------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par AVG OCT  19\tab 34\tab   25\tab    14\tab  3\tab  5\par AVG SEP  22\tab 36\tab   20\tab    14\tab  2\tab  6\par AVG AUG  23\tab 36\tab   21\tab    15\tab  2\tab  4\par AVG JUL  19\tab 39\tab   22\tab    13\tab  3\tab  4\par AVG JUN  21\tab 37\tab   23\tab    12\tab  3\tab  5\par AVG MAY  27\tab 30\tab   23\tab    11\tab  3\tab  5\par AVG APR  27\tab 29\tab   23\tab    12\tab  2\tab  6\par AVG MAR  30\tab 27\tab   18\tab    11\tab  8\tab  6\par AVG FEB  30\tab 28\tab   23\tab    12\tab  3\tab  4\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab   TREAS    CORP    MORTGAGE    AGENCY   CASH   OTHR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1999------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par AVG DEC  35\tab 23\tab   21\tab    15\tab  5\tab  2\par AVG OCT  16\tab 40\tab   15\tab    16\tab  4\tab  9\par AVG AUG  29\tab 27\tab   15\tab    18\tab  7\tab  5\par AVG APR  22\tab 34\tab   26\tab     6\tab  4\tab  8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par GB/ASSET - Reuters British-based asset allocation survey\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JP/ASSET - Reuters Tokyo-based asset allocation survey\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EUR/ASSET - Reuters Europe-based asset allocation survey\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By Andrew Priest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEW YORK, Oct 27 (Reuters) - U.S.-based fund managers are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keeping their global bets steady, reluctant to shift out of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shaky U.S. stock markets over the last month while the euro is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still sliding.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll of 11 U.S. asset allocators, conducted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday through Thursday and released on Friday, found fund\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par managers shaved their average allocations to U.S. equities to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44 percent of global stock portfolios from 45 percent in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par September's survey and doubled cash positions to 4 percent from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite the convulsions in U.S. stock markets which sent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par technology shares skidding lower on worries about the pace of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par profit growth, further crumpling of the European single\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made it unappealing for U.S. funds to shift cash\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par across the Atlantic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Allocations to European shares remain little changed and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fund managers kept their holdings of Japanese shares unchanged\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after three of months of cutting back bets there.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Over the last month, the U.S. Nasdaq composite has tumbled\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 19.6 percent, the Dow Jones industrial average has fallen 7.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent, the Japanese Nikkei 225 index has slid 13.5 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the Dow Jones STOXX index has fallen 6.0 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the euro has fallen 7.8 percent over the last two\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par months against the dollar. This brings its total losses for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year to 19.2 percent. For U.S. funds this would have easily\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par wiped out any positive returns in European markets this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Group of 20 finance ministers communique made no mention\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the euro's plight on Wednesday and a solitary comment from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mexican Finance Minister Jose Angel Gurria that the G20 agreed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the euro was misaligned did little to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slide.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Group of Seven top industrial nations spent up to an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par estimated $6 billion Sept. 22 to buy euros in a bid to halt its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par precipitous decline, but the euro soon resumed its stately\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downward progression.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market speculation about U.S. participation in fresh\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been rife since European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par President Wim Duisenberg, in a newspaper interview last week,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appeared to play down the prospects of near-term \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and seemed to encourage the view that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 United States\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not join in any more euro-supportive action.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Charles Van Vleet, senior fund manager at Credit Suisse\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par First Boston, said one of the main reasons for the euro's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued fall was the size of the U.S. capital account deficit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which reflected huge foreign direct investment by European\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par companies in the United States.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "To see the euro recover you are going to have to see\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe stop buying so much in the U.S., not the U.S. buying in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It doesn't seem that the market is very bunched up on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short side against the euro. It's pretty unlikely that the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would catch many offside if they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par makes it less likely to be successful," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most fund managers are underweight U.S. stocks vs. the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Morgan Stanley Capital International World Index, a well\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par followed benchmark stock index which gives recommended\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par allocations to global bourses based on relative market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capitalisation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Economic data stretching back to late May has raised hopes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par among investors that the Fed's interest rate tightening cycle\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which began in June 1999 has succeeded in slowing the giant $10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trillion U.S. economy to a sustainable pace and removing the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par need for additional rate hikes. Rates currently stand at 6.50\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. government data released on Thursday showed the pay\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and benefits of workers rose modestly in the third quarter of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the year, in a report likely to further comfort the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflation-wary Federal Reserve.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwar03bcw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
