\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-G7 euro  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen a question of when, not if. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Swaha Pattanaik \par \uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2000\par 13:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 26 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers know the Group of Seven nations will eventually act in defence of the battered euro, as they did a month ago, but believe a repeat rescue mission is getting held up by differences over timing. \par \par \uc2  Record lows near 82.3 cents which the euro hit against the dollar on Thursday are more than four cents below levels it was at when the G7 went on a joint euro-buying spree on September 22 and down 30 percent from its January 1999 launch. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the world's richest countries could not afford to allow the euro's slide to continue without eventually putting up some resistance given they have already said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall posed a potential threat to the world economy. \par \par \uc2  But differences of opinion within the G7 about the best time to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again are seen as the most likely explanation for why it has not mounted another joint defence of the euro, with the U.S. Presidential elections looming and market conditions not necessarily conducive to easy success. \par \par \uc2  This has left dealers free to bet against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The G7 will be looking at things closely and everyone in the G7 knows that if \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to work it cannot be a one-off shot," said Avinash Persaud, head of global research at State Street in London. \par \par \uc2  "But it may be harder to get an agreement on the timing." \par \par \uc2  U.S. POLITICS A SPANNER IN THE WORKS \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose involvement in the last round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shocked traders, is seen as one of the key stumbling blocks to renewed G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon. \par \par \uc2  Traders are betting that the U.S. administration will be reluctant to weaken the dollar too significantly with the U.S. Presidential elections less than two weeks away, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The strength of the dollar, whose highs against the euro correspond to its best levels against the deutsche mark since 1986, is taking a heavy toll on U.S. firms' competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  But a marked retreat in the dollar could undermine international confidence in U.S. stocks and bonds, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "People do not believe the U.S. is going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the elections - if they sold dollars and this led to a sell-off in the Dow it would cause political problems for the administration," said Tony Norfield, head of global treasury research at ABN Amro in London. \par \par \uc2  "It looks likely that we will get to $0.80." \par \par \uc2  BEAR TRAP OR MISSED OPPORTUNITY? \par \par \uc2  Speculation that G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro's support was not imminent was sparked after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg said in a newspaper interview published earlier this month that the Group would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if a crisis in the Middle East caused a sharp fall in the euro's value. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg and other international policymakers have since tried to revive the spectre of euro-supportive action by warning that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was always a weapon in their armoury. \par \par \uc2  But traders have been unimpressed as they have yet to follow their words up with more action. \par \par \uc2  They said said there was always the possibility that the G7's absence from the foreign exchanges could be designed to lull the foreign exchanges into a false sense of security and cause euro bears maximum pain. \par \par \uc2  This was seen as the case back in September when the G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the day before they met in Prague rather than acting after their meeting. \par \par \uc2  But \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said leaving the euro to fall too far before they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a risky strategy. \par \par \uc2  "They would be foolhardy if they thought they could lull the market into a false sense of security," said Colin Clarkson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Sumitomo Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "If it goes below $0.80 they will really have to start worrying as people will say they have just lost the plot. They may have to step up to the plate shortly." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwaq03gcu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
