\par\par \b \uc2  Tumbling euro finds fragile floor in Tokyo. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 785 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2000\par 05:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 19 (Reuters) - The euro found a fragile floor in Tokyo on Thursday after careening off another steep cliff against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight, but few expected the floor to hold. \par \par \uc2  Nervous short-covering held the bruised \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above $0.8400 at one point in morning trade, up from a record low of $0.8324 on EBS hit in New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The short-covering emerged as a storm of official comments on the euro left dealers wary about the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly given that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) policy board meets later in the day and its president, Wim Duisenberg, is to hold a crucial news conference after the meeting. \par \par \uc2  The signs were ominous for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after its breach of a previous lifetime low of $0.8440. \par \par \uc2  "I don't see even a single euro-supportive factor now, other than the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ryohei Muramatsu, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Commerzbank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "A record low of $0.8324 was just a passing point, and we can no longer predict where the euro's bottom is," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was hovering at $0.8397/02 compared with $0.8388 in late New York on Wednesday, but market talk is focusing on a visit to 82 cents or 80 cents in the short term. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at 90.50/64 yen but dealers are expecting possible Japanese offers above 90.50/60 and are focusing on a New York low of around 89.50 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro was pummelled in New York despite a more than 400-point fall in the Dow Jones industrial average at one point. \par \par \uc2  The euro initially tried to pick itself up on the back of plunging U.S. stocks, but as the topside proved stern and stocks began to rebound from lows, speculators soon joined in and hammered the euro back down again, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Further hurting the euro were comments on Wednesday by U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers reiterating his stance that a strong dollar remains in the U.S. national interest. \par \par \uc2  This was seen as a blow to the euro, as the ECB's Duisenberg was reported to have asked Summers to modify the language of the policy to something more euro-friendly. \par \par \uc2  "Whether Duisenberg will be pressured to resign is one focus," said a dealer at a major Japanese bank, adding his resignation would further batter the euro. \par \par \uc2  Summers also said the recent Group of Seven (G7) statement reflects the U.S. position on exchange rates, suggesting his country is still open to coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although he declined to comment directly on whether the G7 would support another round of action in the market. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said volatility in the U.S. equity markets - in part blamed on the euro's weakness - would seem to give the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  reason to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I see no reason why the U.S. can't join in," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials were also busy putting in their two cents on the euro. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said he was closely watching the euro, although he added he has not heard anything from euro-zone authorities about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In a rare move, Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami also said the G7 will take appropriate action on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed. \par \par \uc2  "All these comments are holding the market back from pushing the euro down for now, but I think it's just a matter of time before the euro jumps off a cliff again," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Weakness in the euro/yen cross weighed on the dollar against the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 107.73/83 yen with bids seen under 107.50 and offers at 108.10. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0307 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   18 Oct.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab   0.8398   0.8388   +0.12   -16.60   1.0070\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab    107.74   107.66   +0.07    +5.41   102.21\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab    90.46    90.38   +0.09   -12.26   103.10\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.7866   1.7868   -0.01   +12.35   1.5902\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.4451   1.4433   +0.12   -10.66   1.6176\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab    1.5155   1.5166   -0.07    +4.84   1.4455\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.5187   0.5203   -0.31   -20.97   0.6563\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab 1.5011   1.5004   +0.05    -6.39   1.6036\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.5806   0.5806   +0.00    -6.94   0.6239.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwaj040nt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
