\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro prays for G7 shelter amid selling storm. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wayne Cole \par \uc2 965 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2000\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 19 (Reuters) - The euro was in danger of sinking from sight on Thursday after a tidal wave of selling swept it to lifetime lows. \par \par \uc2  Only the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  afloat at $0.8395 in Tokyo after it tumbled three percent on Wednesday to a lifetime low at $0.8324 according to dealers, a full cent beneath its previous trough of $0.8440. \par \par \uc2  It also suffered all-time lows on the yen and Swiss franc while the dollar rocketed to a 14-year high on the franc and made record peaks on the Australian and New Zealand dollars. \par \par \uc2  The euro's headlong flight drew a chorus of comment from European, U.S. and Japanese officials that the Group of Seven industrial powers stood ready to act in the market. \par \par \uc2  Most importantly U.S. Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers spoke up to say the U.S. stance was the same as in the G7 communique which followed the September 22 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He confused the issue somewhat, however, by repeating word for word the old mantra that a strong dollar was in the national interests of the United States. \par \par \uc2  Dealers took this as a slap in the face for European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg who had asked Summers to modify the language of the policy so that it was friendlier toward the euro. \par \par \uc2  And it was Duisenberg and his future that most concerned the market now as investors waited for today's ECB news conference to see if he could rescue the euro, and perhaps his career with it. \par \par \uc2  "They've raised rates and it didn't work. They've \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it didn't work. People want to see a radically different policy," said Ken Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank, adding that the most effective stance would be to sharply curb euro zone liquidity and so the supply of euros. \par \par \uc2  "But there's no sign the ECB is willing to take such steps, so the euro stands condemned," he concluded. \par \par \uc2  Landin also argued that Wednesday's events proved \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a flawed response to the euro's woes. \par \par \uc2  "What they did was create a speculative bubble as people bought the euro in expectation of yet more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. "What we saw yesterday was that bubble bursting." \par \par \uc2  The breaking point came when Wall Street rallied sharply from deep early lows, catching the interbank market long of euros up at $0.8570. That tripped stop-loss sell orders under 85 cents and again at $0.8460 and in turn encouraged speculative selling by a mob of momentum and black box funds. \par \par \uc2  They trampled over the previous record low at $0.8440 and took out massive options positions at 84 cents, triggering yet more distressed selling and taking it as low as $0.8324 on EBS. \par \par \uc2  The entire move took just two hours. \par \par \uc2  At the same time the euro sank to lifetime lows on the yen, falling all the way from 92.00 yen to crater at 89.50, and on the Swiss franc deep under 1.5000 francs. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted with some amusement that the euro hit record lows on such \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the Lithuanian litas and the Kazakhstan tenge, so challenging the usual excuse of euro zone officials that its weakness was all due to dollar strength. \par \par \uc2  Which is not to say the dollar isn't strong. It too made a 14-year high on the Swiss franc at 1.7990 francs and against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - as measured by the FINEX futures trade-weighted contract - it jumped to decade highs. \par \par \uc2  And this strength was starting to have repercussions. For one thing it was forcing inflation and interest rates higher in those countries with weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , threatening global growth. \par \par \uc2  Closer to home, it has been cited by numerous U.S. corporations as a drag on earnings and contributed to the slump in equity prices. \par \par \uc2  Even officials at the Federal Reserve, who normally leave \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  comments to the Treasury, had began to sound edgy. San Francisco Fed President Robert Parry on Wednesday became the second member of the Fed's policy-making arm this week to mention that the strong dollar was dampening domestic production and hurting exports. \par \par \uc2  All of which led analysts to suspect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  might see enough domestic reasons to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro, if only as a gesture to investors in all markets that the G7 was watching. \par \par \uc2  But again dealers warned this would only provide short-term succour. \par \par \uc2  "The G7's offering a sticking plaster when the euro needs open heart surgery," said a European bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "While they mess around, the market's got its mind set on 80 cents. There's supposed to be a mountain of option positions there, which would make all the bears happy." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0554 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   1999 Cls\par \tab