\par\par \b \uc2  IMM  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  end down, stocks pressure contracts. \b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Oktober 2000\par 22:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CHICAGO, Oct 13 U.S. stocks came roaring back to knock most IMM \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures lower on Friday, as the December euro sank to its lowest level since last month's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  December euros declined steadily over the session, falling to a $0.85550 daily low. The \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan and Europe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  jointly on September 22 when the contract hit an $0.86010 session low. \par \par \uc2  After steep declines on Thursday, the Nasdaq composite rose more than 7 percent and the Dow Jones Industrial Average more than 1.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The rebound in U.S. stock market is an added reason to unwind any kind of trades people put on for fear that this is going to make for an immediate collapse of the U.S. economy, which is ridiculous," said David Ethridge, director of capital market strategy at Standard & Poor's. \par \par \uc2  With euro futures back to levels before the central banks' action, market analysts were talking about the possibility of another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The markets (want) to test the resolve of the G7 to see if and when they will come back in and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  together," said Lisa Conte, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Prudential Securities. \par \par \uc2  November crude oil futures stabilised slightly, pulling back from Thursday's $37 contract high sparked by conflict in the Middle East including an attack on a U.S. naval ship. Some players may have unwound safe-haven trades in the Swiss franc, and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well, after oil slipped, Ethridge said. \par \par \uc2  "One news item from the Gulf that is worse than the previous ones, and we're right back to where we were before, for those people that trade on a very near-term basis," Ethridge said. \par \par \uc2  December yen settled $0.000027 lower at $0.009382, euros closed off $0.00910 at $0.85640, Swiss francs were off $0.0091 at $0.5682, sterling fell $0.0184 to $1.4536, Mexican pesos were up $0.000350 at $0.103775, Australian dollars were down $0.0033 at $0.5295, and Canadian dollars were up $0.0012 at $0.6644. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010822dwad0495u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
