\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro dented as market tests ECB's resolve. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 605 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2000\par 09:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 6 (Reuters) - The euro fell to its lowest against the dollar on Friday since last month's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after a surprise euro zone rate hike a day ago failed to stop the market from pushing the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said market disappointment the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not used the rally in euro/dollar after Thursday's rate hike as an opportunity to repeat the joint Group of Seven \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of September 22 had helped push the euro lower. \par \par \uc2  Still, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters remained and were heightened by comments from ECB President Wim Duisenberg after the rate hike on Thursday, that all members of the G7, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cooperate on more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it was needed. \par \par \uc2  "There was an expectation that we could have seen some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the rate hike. Part of the reason for yesterday's rise in the euro was on that fact and when we didn't see it, the market sold off," said Mitul Kotecha, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Credit Agricole Indosuez in London. \par \par \uc2  "We fell below \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels so there is an increasing risk over the next few days that the ECB will come back in to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  The euro had drifted off lows around $0.8675, down more than one percent from peaks around $0.8790 set immediately after Thursday's ECB rate hike. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was trading around 94.80, having fallen to one-week lows earlier just above 94.40. \par \par \uc2  Rate hikes can sometimes support a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by improving the returns on deposits, but in this case analysts said the market was more worried it was overkill for the euro zone economy at a time when many forward indicators were pointing to a slowdown. \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg claimed the rate rise would support growth, but to no avail. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB view is contradicted by analysts from all quarters (saying) the economy has likely peaked and will slow in the face of higher oil prices, which is a de-facto tightening," Karl Broeker, head of Treasury at Landesbank Baden-Wuerttenberg in Singapore, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN EARTHQUAKE \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the yen had firmed slightly against the dollar, towards 108.70 but remained within one percent of Thursday's seven-week peaks. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said concerns following news an earthquake with a magnitude of 7.1 on the open-ended Richter scale rocked broad areas of western Japan on Friday were adding pressure to the yen but had not so far had a significant impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The damage to the yen on Friday was somewhat limited, as the quake hit mostly rural areas of Japan, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had so far failed to gain ground lost after the event. \par \par \uc2  The minutes of the Federal Open Market Committee's August meeting, released on Thursday, said, "The statistical evidence reviewed by the committee...pointed to a noticeable slowing in the expansion of demand and economic activity". \par \par \uc2  The market was now waiting for a September U.S. employment report later on Friday. The jobless rate is seen steady at 4.1 percent, while average hourly earnings should rise a moderate 0.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  "U.S data is very important because the U.S. Fed has expressed concern about the tightness of the labour market," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, economist at CIBC World Markets. \par \par \uc2  "If we get a strong number, it will bring nervousness in the market and it may help the euro." \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Australian dollar fell to a record trough around $0.5280, partly in sympathy with the weak euro. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa6056qr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
