\par\par \b \uc2  Weak euro not hurting US but Fed watching it - official. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Genevieve Wilkinson \par \uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2000\par 23:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MT. POCONO, Pa., Oct. 5 (Reuters) - Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia President Anthony Santomero said on Thursday the sickly euro has not yet hurt the U.S. economy, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keeping a close eye on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "At the moment the euro has not substantially affected the real sector, but we are looking closely and will continue to monitor this closely," Santomero said after addressing the Pocono Northeast Regional Workforce Development Summit. \par \par \uc2  The newly appointed Fed official also said that recent figures point to a slowing of the fast-paced U.S. economy, which posted 5.6 percent annual growth in the second quarter. \par \par \uc2  But the Fed remains alert to any inflationary pressures from rising oil prices and labour markets, he added. \par \par \uc2  "Our position has been, and I think it is substantiated by the bulk of data, that economic growth has slowed somewhat," Santomero said. \par \par \uc2  His words echoed a Fed statement issued on Tuesday when it voted to leave official U.S. rates unchanged at 6.50 percent but warned inflationary risks remain. \par \par \uc2  The United States surprised markets two weeks ago when it joined Group of Seven central banks in a buying spree to support the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has shed about 25 percent of its value since its birth in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  At the time, policy officials cited the risks to the global economy from a weak European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in making the decision to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  For the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro's drop has hurt earnings from major companies, including Intel Corp., Dell Computer Corp. and Eastman Kodak Co., while U.S. manufacturers are starting to complain the strong dollar makes their exports too expensive. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped again on Thursday to lows not seen since the Sept. 22 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the decline coming despite the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise decision to raise its official interest rates by one quarter percentage point to 4.75 percent. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate hikes typically buoy a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Santomero, who was appointed Philadelphia Fed president in June replacing Edward Boehne, is a nonvoting member of the Federal Reserve's rate-setting Federal Open Market Committee. He is a former finance professor at the University of Pennsylvania's prestigious Wharton School of Business. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dwa5055t9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
