\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro sits tight in Asia, market respectful of G7. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 607 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2000\par 09:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 26 (Reuters) - The euro was trapped in tight ranges against the yen and the dollar in Tokyo on Tuesday, with traders reluctant to challenge the Group of Seven's (G7) commitment to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  afloat. \par \par \uc2  In typically nervous post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, players were unwilling to take new euro positions ahead of Thursday's Danish referendum on joining the euro. \par \par \uc2  "Even if people wanted to, nobody can sell euro now particularly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and ahead of the Danish vote," a Japanese commercial bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  A "no" vote by Danes is likely to deal a fresh blow to confidence in the euro, but the latest opinion poll published by national TV news on Tuesday showed opponents of Danish membership losing some of their lead over supporters. \par \par \uc2  The Megafon poll gave opponents a five-point lead, down from six in a Monday evening poll and compared with an 11-point lead on Sunday. \par \par \uc2  "The euro could come under renewed selling pressure if Denmark rejects the euro and that will be the moment to judge the G7 nations and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's determination to prevent it sliding," he said. \par \par \uc2  Despite a strong G7 statement of their commitment to stabilising the euro following Friday's surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some operators still doubt the eagerness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the euro at the expense of its long-standing "strong dollar" policy. \par \par \uc2  At 0542 GMT, the euro traded very quietly at $0.8740/45 near late U.S. levels, with support at $0.8740 and $0.8712 and resistance around $0.8780. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at 93.90/99 yen having eased to about 93.80 yen in the morning, and traders were looking to test the overnight low of 93.65 yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa issued a warning to the market on Tuesday morning, implying there is a risk of further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The G7 statement clearly said the G7 would take action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. I want the market to judge from that statement," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  As of 0552 GMT, the dollar stood at 107.35/45 yen compared with Monday's late U.S. level of 107.73/81 yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen was generally supported against the dollar and the euro on sporadic yen-buying led from exporters, but activity was thin as other Japanese operators were sidelined ahead of interim fiscal bookclosings on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar/yen rate is clearly out of the market's focus now until the tankan data next week. Presently, the rate is being moved by the supply-demand balance and the fluctuations in the euro/yen rate," a Japanese trust bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan is scheduled to release its quarterly "tankan" business sentiment survey next Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Yen-supportive news emerged on Monday from ratings agency Standard and Poor's Corp (S&P), which said it saw no reason to downgrade Japan's sovereign debt rating from its current top triple-A status. \par \par \uc2  "S&P's view is that Japan continues to be of the highest credit status," David Beers, managing director for sovereign ratings at S&P, told reporters at a briefing on the fringes of the annual International Monetary Fund and World Bank meetings in Prague. \par \par \uc2  Citing worries about the nation's huge debt levels, Moody's Investors Service recently downgraded its rating for domestic yen-denominated bonds issued by the Japanese government to Aa2 from Aa1, putting the rating two notches below S&P's. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9q06kr9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
