\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro kept afloat amid nervousness of G7. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 787 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2000\par 14:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Sept 26 (Reuters) - The euro was buoyed across the board on Tuesday amid wariness that the Group of Seven may again step in to support the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following joint \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend it last week. \par \par \uc2  The market's nervousness was highlighted when the euro staged a swift rebound, racking up gains of half a yen and more than a third of a cent within minutes, after falling towards levels at which G7 central banks took action on Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wariness was later underlined after comments from the head of the International Monetary Fund Horst Koehler briefly pushed the euro to test its day's highs. \par \par \uc2  Koehler said that balanced exchange rates were needed and Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at bringing the euro more into line with fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Luxembourg \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Yves Mersch said that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had all the necessary ammunition for further \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it was needed. \par \par \uc2  "At some stage the G7 will come in again. The market seems to be suggesting a move below $0.86 towards $0.85 would be the impetus for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action again," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mistubishi in London. \par \par \uc2  The euro was within half a cent of its day's high at $0.8800 according to Reuters data, up around four percent from last week's record lows around $0.8440. However, it was still down more than two cents from Friday's post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highs. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was orbiting 94 yen, up more than four yen from last weeks' record lows. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the ECB's weekly money market tender was inconclusive on the amount of Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that might have been sterilised but the higher than expected rates threw the focus forwards to Thursday's ECB policy meeting. \par \par \uc2  The ECB alloted refis in variable tender at a 4.65 percent marginal rate and a 4.68 percent average rate, compared with last week's rates of 4.56 and 4.58 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2  "It is difficult to ascertain the amount sterilised (from the ECB refi auction). The interest rate move up was a bit higher than people had expected and the key will be Thursday when there is a reasonable chance that we will get something," said Halpenny at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  DANISH REFERENDUM A FOCUS \par \par \uc2  Caution ahead of Thursday's Danish referendum on euro entry was also said to be supporting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said that while a "no" vote by the Danes would probably deal a fresh blow to confidence in the euro, latest opinion polls showed that Danish euro opponents' lead over supporters had been shrinking. \par \par \uc2  "There is still a lot of uncertainty on the Danish referendum and on the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Roberto Mialich, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Unicredit in Milan. \par \par \uc2  "We have to wait for the market reaction to the Danish referendum. Right now the market is betting on a 'no' and although this outcome is already partially priced in, people could start selling the euro anyway to test the central banks' resolve." \par \par \uc2  Senior G7 officials continued to keep the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the forefront of the market's mind. \par \par \uc2  Luxembourg's Prime Minister and Finance Minister Jean-Claude Juncker told Reuters that the G7 had sent a clear message to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets through Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it wanted a stronger euro. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa issued a warning to the market earlier on Tuesday of the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the euro plunges again. \par \par \uc2  Despite a strong G7 statement of their commitment to stabilising the euro following Friday's surprise joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said the the \b \highlight22\uc2 United States\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the most reluctant participant in Friday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the U.S. authorities commitment to its long-standing "strong dollar" policy. \par \par \uc2  "Because U.S. policy of a strong dollar has been maintained, and the possibility that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't sizeable on Friday, it would suggest that they are more just trying to stem the decline rather than turn the euro around and boost it higher, which could undermine growth in the euro zone," Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi's Halpenny said. \par \par \uc2  He said euro/dollar could therefore range trade between $0.86 and $0.90 for some time. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar softened against a generally firmer yen in thin trading ahead of the release of the Bank of Japan's quarterly "tankan" business sentiment survey next Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to around 107.20 yen, down about a yen from Friday's one-month highs around 108.15 yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9q06deo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
